      "name": "AudioThreadWorker",
      "signature": "DWORD AudioThreadWorker(void * pUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Audio thread worker that processes sound objects and manages audio playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Wait on g_hAudioEvent with 50ms timeout (0x32)\n2. If wait returns non-WAIT_TIMEOUT (0x102), exit thread with return 0\n3. Enter g_hSoundCriticalSection for thread-safe access\n4. Store previous mute state, update g_dwSoundMute based on window iconic state\n5. Check sound queue timing via GetLastSoundQueueTime\n6. If queue active and audio object invalid, restart background music\n7. Iterate through sound object linked list (g_dwObjectPoolLock)\n8. For each sound object:\n   a. Call SAudCloseStreamAndCleanup for pending cleanup\n   b. If mute state changed, recalculate and apply volume\n   c. Process volume fade transitions (fields +0x13 to +0x17)\n   d. Handle streaming audio position updates\n   e. Manage circular buffer wraparound\n   f. Write new data to sound buffer via WriteSoundBufferData\n9. Leave critical section\n10. Loop back to step 1 (infinite loop)\n\nParameters:\n  lpParameter: Thread parameter (unused, always NULL from CreateThread)\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD: 0 when thread exits (signaled via event timeout)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertion failures if sound buffer pointers are NULL\n  - Volume fade interpolation: lerp between +0x14 (start) and +0x15 (end) over time window +0x16 to +0x17\n  - Streaming audio uses SAudCloseStream for cleanup\n  - Non-streaming uses DirectSound buffer lock/unlock via vtable offsets +0x2c/+0x4c\n\nSound Object Structure Layout:\n  Offset  | Size | Field Name        | Type    | Description\n  --------|------|-------------------|---------|------------------------------------------\n  +0x00   | 4    | pDirectSoundBuf   | IDS*    | DirectSound buffer interface pointer\n  +0x04   | 4    | dwBufferSize      | uint    | Sound buffer size in bytes\n  +0x08   | 4    | dwPlayPosition    | uint    | Current playback position\n  +0x14   | 4    | nFadeStartVol     | int     | Volume fade start value\n  +0x18   | 4    | nFadeEndVol       | int     | Volume fade target value\n  +0x1c   | 4    | dwFadeStartTime   | DWORD   | Fade start tick count\n  +0x20   | 4    | dwFadeEndTime     | DWORD   | Fade end tick count\n  +0x34   | 4    | dwFlags           | uint    | Sound flags (bit 2 = spatial audio)\n  +0x38   | 4    | nCurrentVolume    | int     | Current volume level (0-255)\n  +0x48   | 4    | hStreamHandle     | HANDLE  | Streaming audio handle (0 if not streaming)\n  +0x4c   | 4    | fFadeActive       | int     | Non-zero if volume fade in progress\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x32: 50ms wait timeout for audio event\n  - 0x102: WAIT_TIMEOUT constant\n  - 0xff: Volume scaling divisor (255 max volume)\n  - 0x3c: DirectSound SetVolume vtable offset\n  - 0x48: DirectSound Stop vtable offset\n  - 0x2c: DirectSound Lock vtable offset\n  - 0x4c: DirectSound Unlock vtable offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:2b0fb5fd699684d6bfafc11b18be73ae",
