      "name": "InitializeAudioStream",
      "signature": "uint InitializeAudioStream(int nAudioHandle, int nStreamFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes audio stream with specified flags and parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify global audio object exists (g_pAudioGameObject != NULL)\n2. Check audio stream state via GetMaskedVolumeFactor\n3. Validate stream initialization status via IsStateValid\n4. If state invalid and audio handle provided, initialize sample\n5. Set initial volume to 0x6e (110 dB)\n6. Open audio stream with flags and parameters\n7. Return success/failure based on stream open result\n\nParameters:\n- nAudioHandle (ECX): Audio handle flag, must be non-zero to proceed\n- nStreamFlags (EDX): Stream initialization flags passed to OpenAudioStream\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Stream opened successfully\n- 0: Audio object NULL, state check failed, or stream open failed\n\nRelated: GetMaskedVolumeFactor, IsStateValid, InitSoundSample, SetSoundVolume, OpenAudioStream",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:4601bb33bcc083889b2ce69d9e1684d9",
