      "name": "LinkedListAppendNode",
      "signature": "void LinkedListAppendNode(int * pListHead, dword dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Appends a new node to the end of a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8-byte node via FogMemAlloc\n2. Initialize node fields to zero\n3. Store dwValue in first field of node\n4. Traverse linked list from pListHead following next pointers (+4 offset)\n5. Find last node (where next pointer is 0)\n6. If list is empty, make new node the head\n7. If list has elements, link last node to new node\n\nParameters:\n- pListHead (int*): Pointer to linked list head (updated with new node if list was empty)\n- dwValue (dword): Value to store in new node's first field\n\nReturns:\n- void (function modifies linked list in-place, no return value)",
