      "name": "RoundToNearestInteger",
      "signature": "void RoundToNearestInteger(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if FPU ST0 register value is already rounded to nearest integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Duplicate ST0 and round copy with FRNDINT\n2. Compare rounded value to original\n3. If equal, return (value already rounded)\n4. Otherwise increment CL counter and retry once more with FMUL scaling\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains float10 value to check\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies FPU stack and CL register as side effects)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Log2F64: Caller that uses result via CL register for rounding adjustments",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:634f5fd2b38b5a9728c3cfaee438889f",
