      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles initialization and cleanup of the manager subsystem.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nState==1: Initialize manager (version check, registry setup, command-line parsing, callback setup)\n2. If nState==0: Shutdown manager (decrement counter, cleanup, finalize)\n3. If nState==3: Handle special request with null pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nFlags (int): Control flags (unused in main logic)\n- nState (int): Operation code (1=init, 0=shutdown, 3=special)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful operation\n- 0 on failure or inactive state",
