      "name": "CleanupManagerContext",
      "signature": "void CleanupManagerContext(void * pManagerContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Cleanup and release manager context resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify TLS slot is initialized (not -1), exit if invalid\n2. If pManagerContext is NULL, retrieve context pointer from TLS storage\n3. If context is still NULL, skip cleanup and go to TLS clear\n4. Iterate through fixed field offsets in context: 0x24, 0x28, 0x30, 0x38, 0x40, 0x44, 0x50\n5. For each non-NULL field pointer, call cleanup function FUN_6f9e79bf()\n6. Free context structure itself via FUN_6f9e79bf()\n7. Clear TLS slot to NULL via TlsSetValue()\n\nParameters:\n- pManagerContext (void *): Pointer to manager context structure or NULL to fetch from TLS\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xffffffff: Invalid TLS slot sentinel value\n- 0x24, 0x28, 0x30, 0x38, 0x40, 0x44, 0x50: Field offsets within context structure containing resource pointers",
