      "name": "Exp2F64",
      "signature": "float10 Exp2F64(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, double dExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes 2^x (base-2 exponential) using x87 FPU instructions.\n\nThis is part of the C runtime math library implementation for exp2().\nUses F2XM1 and FSCALE FPU instructions for accurate computation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize status byte at [EBP-0x90] to 0xFE (special case marker)\n2. Check if exponent high byte is non-zero (special value check)\n3. If special value, call validation function at 0x6f9e69b1\n4. If validation returns 0, return negative infinity constant\n5. Otherwise call reduction function at 0x6f9e696e to get fractional part\n6. Add 1 to result (F2XM1 computes 2^x - 1, so add 1 for 2^x)\n7. Check flag at [EBP-0x9F] bit 0 for negative exponent handling\n8. If negative and SSE available (g_dwProcessorFeatureResult==1), use SSE path\n9. If negative without SSE, compute reciprocal (1/result)\n10. If DL bit 6 clear, apply FSCALE with integer part from ST1\n11. If sign flag (CH) non-zero, negate result\n12. Return extended precision result\n\nParameters:\ndExponent - double precision exponent value (passed on stack)\nIMPLICIT: __return_storage_ptr__ in ECX for float10 return\n\nReturns:\nfloat10 - Extended precision result of 2^dExponent\n\nGlobals Referenced:\ng_dwProcessorFeatureResult (0x6f9f3d6c) - CPU feature detection result (1=SSE available)\ng_ldNegativeInfinity (0x6f9f0d30) - Negative infinity constant for special cases\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns negative infinity for invalid/overflow inputs\n- Uses SSE optimization path when processor supports it\n- Handles negative exponents via reciprocal or SSE division\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Log2F64: Inverse operation (logarithm base 2)\n- InitializeCpuAndFpFeatures: Sets g_dwProcessorFeatureResult",
