      "name": "Exp2F64ReduceFraction",
      "signature": "float10 Exp2F64ReduceFraction(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Reduces exponent to fractional part for F2XM1 instruction in exp2() computation.\n\nThis is the reduction phase of the base-2 exponential function. It separates the \ninput exponent into integer and fractional parts, then applies F2XM1 to the \nfractional part. F2XM1 only works correctly for inputs in the range [-1, +1].\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Duplicate ST0 (input exponent) and take absolute value\n2. Load threshold constant g_ldF2xm1Threshold (32768.0)\n3. Compare |exponent| against threshold using FCOMPP\n4. If |exponent| >= threshold (special case), jump to overflow handler at 0x6f9e6920\n5. Otherwise, duplicate ST0 and apply FRNDINT to get integer part\n6. Test if integer part is zero and save FPU status flags to DL\n7. Subtract integer part from original to get fractional part: frac = x - round(x)\n8. Take absolute value of fractional part (F2XM1 requires non-negative input)\n9. Apply F2XM1 to compute 2^|frac| - 1\n10. Return with ST0 = 2^|frac| - 1, ST1 = integer part, DL = sign flags\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT: ST0 (in_ST0) - Extended precision exponent value to reduce\nIMPLICIT: EBP (unaff_EBP) - Points to stack frame with FPU status word storage at [EBP-0xA0]\n\nReturns:\nST0 - Result of F2XM1(|fractional_part|), which is 2^|frac| - 1\nST1 - Integer part of exponent (for use by FSCALE in caller)\nDL - FPU status flags indicating sign of integer part\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\nfVar1 (ldAbsExponent) - Absolute value of input exponent |ST0|\nfVar2 (ldIntegerPart) - Integer part after FRNDINT\n\nCompiler Artifacts:\n__return_storage_ptr__ - Auto return storage for float10 result\nunaff_retaddr - Return address tracking\n\nGlobals Referenced:\ng_ldF2xm1Threshold (0x6f9f0cee) - 32768.0, max value for standard F2XM1 path\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If |exponent| >= 32768, jumps to overflow handler (large exponent path)\n- Negative exponents handled via absolute value before F2XM1, sign tracked in DL\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Exp2F64: Parent function that calls this for reduction phase\n- FpuDiscardAndReturnZero (0x6f9e6b26): Returns zero for special cases",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
