      "name": "FpuDiscardAndReturnZero",
      "signature": "float10 FpuDiscardAndReturnZero(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Discards FPU ST0 input and returns floating-point zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pop and discard the current ST0 value (FSTP ST0)\n2. Load 0.0 onto the FPU stack (FLDZ)\n3. Return with 0.0 in ST0\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_ST0 (float10): Input value to discard (consumed, not used)\n\nReturns:\n  float10: Always returns 0.0 in ST0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called from Exp2F64ReduceFraction when input is negative after 2^x\n    fraction processing, indicating underflow to zero\n  - Part of exponential computation error handling path\n\nClassification: Leaf function - FPU utility for math library",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:038f21ccadf05fbd1bec4c0181e46e90",
