      "name": "ReturnNegativeInfinityF64",
      "signature": "undefined1[10] ReturnNegativeInfinityF64(undefined1[10] * __return_storage_ptr__)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns negative infinity (float10) for Exp2F64 overflow/invalid cases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear FPU stack by popping ST0 twice (FSTP ST0 x2)\n2. Load negative infinity constant from g_ldNegativeInfinity (0x6f9f0d30)\n3. Check status flag at caller's [EBP-0x90]\n4. If status flag <= 0, set it to 1 (mark error handled)\n5. Set zero flag via OR CL,CL (affects caller's condition checks)\n6. Return with negative infinity in ST0\n\nParameters:\nNone explicit (accesses caller's stack frame via unaff_EBP)\nIMPLICIT: EBP from caller's frame (accesses [EBP-0x90] status byte)\nIMPLICIT: CL register (set to indicate result state)\n\nReturns:\nfloat10 - Negative infinity constant (-inf) in ST0/FPU register\n\nGlobals Referenced:\ng_ldNegativeInfinity (0x6f9f0d30) - Extended precision -infinity constant\n\nCaller:\nExp2F64 - Called when exponent validation fails (iVar2 == 0)\n\nClassification: Leaf/internal utility function\n\nNotes:\n- The OR CL,CL instruction sets flags for caller's subsequent conditional\n- Status byte at [EBP-0x90] tracks special case handling state in Exp2F64\n- Uses caller's stack frame directly (non-standard calling convention artifact)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
