      "name": "HandleLog2Underflow",
      "signature": "int HandleLog2Underflow(int nValueLo, int nValueHi, double dThreshold, double * pdResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Handles edge cases in log2 calculation for underflow conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute absolute value of 64-bit input (nValueHi:nValueLo)\n2. Check for infinity: if exponent is 0x7ff00000\n   - Handle positive/negative infinity cases\n   - Return special values based on threshold comparisons\n3. Check for negative infinity: if threshold is -INFINITY\n   - Return appropriate log2 value (0 or special value)\n4. For normal cases, compute log2 and store result via pdResult pointer\n5. Return 1 if valid result written, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- nValueLo (int): Low 32 bits of 64-bit input value\n- nValueHi (int): High 32 bits (exponent+sign field) of 64-bit input\n- dThreshold (double): Threshold for comparisons\n- pdResult (double*): Output pointer for result value\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Result successfully computed and written to pdResult\n- 0: Special case handled, result in pdResult or computation incomplete\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Log2F64: Caller function for main log2 computation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:196c90d967af5bf2d30c255ccea793be",
