      "signature": "dword CheckIntegerOrRatio(double dValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Checks if a double value is an integer or a simple fraction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract FPU status flags from the double's upper 32 bits via FUN_6f9e9a81\n2. Check if exponent bits indicate special floating-point state (0x90 mask)\n3. Round the input value and compare with original\n4. If rounded equals original value, it's an integer - return 1\n5. Otherwise divide by 2.0 and round the result\n6. If rounded ratio equals computed ratio, it's a simple fraction - return 2\n7. If none of the above conditions hold - return 0\n\nParameters:\n- dValue (double): Input value to check\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Not an integer or simple fraction\n- 1: Input is an integer (rounds to itself)\n- 2: Input is a simple fraction (e.g., 1.5, 2.25)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x90: FPU exponent status bits indicating special values\n- 2.0 (at 0x6f9ee328): Divisor for checking half-integer ratios\n- Via __frnd: FPU rounding instruction\n\nRelated Functions:\n- HandleLog2Underflow: Caller function\n- FUN_6f9e9a81: Extracts FPU status from double\n- __frnd: FPU round instruction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1252459d5bf6fc7fa6bd21d0f60e6017",
