      "name": "InitializeIOHandles",
      "signature": "void InitializeIOHandles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes standard I/O handle tables from startup info and sets up console handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate initial handle table (0x480 bytes) for stdin/stdout/stderr\n2. Initialize all entries to -1 with control flags\n3. If startup info provides inherited handles, copy them into table\n4. Allocate additional tables if handle count exceeds capacity (0x800 max)\n5. For each unset handle, fetch from GetStdHandle() and cache file type\n6. Set final handle count via SetHandleCount()\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBX used for module state context\n\nReturns:\n- void (initializes global handle table g_puHandleTable, g_dwHandleCount, g_puAdditionalTables)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480 (1152): Handle table allocation size per block\n- 0x120 (288): Entries per table (0x480 / 9 for 9-byte entries)\n- 0x24 (36): Stride between entries in iteration\n- 0x800 (2048): Maximum handle count\n- 0xffffffff: Uninitialized handle sentinel\n- 0xfffffff5-0xfffffff6: Windows STD_*_HANDLE constants",
