      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses command-line argument string into argc/argv format with support for quoted strings and escape sequences.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize argc=1 and character counter\n2. Process leading quoted string (if present) with escape handling\n3. Parse unquoted portion, skipping whitespace and tabs\n4. For each argument, handle backslash escapes and quoted sections\n5. Build argument pointer array and output buffer\n6. Terminate argument list with null pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pszInput (byte*): Input command-line string\n- ppszArgv (dword*): Output array of argument pointers (argv-style)\n- pbOutputBuf (byte*): Output buffer for processed argument strings\n- pnArgc (int*): Output argument count\n- pnCharCount (int*): Output character count processed\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22: Quote character (\")\n- 0x20: Space character\n- 0x09: Tab character\n- 0x5c: Backslash character (\\)\n- 0x04: Character classification flag (whitespace indicator)",
