      "name": "CleanupMemoryAllocations",
      "signature": "void CleanupMemoryAllocations(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up heap and virtual memory allocations based on allocation strategy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check allocation strategy flag (DAT_6f9f42ec)\n2. If strategy==3: Iterate through fixed-size allocation array, free VirtualAlloc blocks, then HeapFree array\n3. If strategy==2: Traverse circular linked list, freeing VirtualAlloc blocks at offset 0x10\n4. Destroy heap object\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f42ec contains allocation strategy (2 or 3)\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f40b4 points to allocation data\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f40b0 contains element count\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f42e8 is heap handle\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100000 (1MB): VirtualAlloc allocation size\n- 0x4000: MEM_DECOMMIT flag\n- 0x8000: MEM_RELEASE flag\n- 0xc: Offset to first allocation pointer in array\n- 0x14 (20): Stride between array elements (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x10 (16): Offset to VirtualAlloc pointer in linked list node",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c2ccec13492440089beaf10a53536424",
