      "name": "HeapAllocWrapper",
      "signature": "void * HeapAllocWrapper(uint * pSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates heap memory with exception handling based on heap version.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current exception handler list\n2. If heap version == 3: Call version-3 allocator (FUN_6f9ea9cb)\n3. If heap version == 2: Round size to 16-byte boundary, call version-2 allocator (FUN_6f9eb178)\n4. Otherwise: Round size to 16-byte boundary, call default HeapAlloc\n5. Restore exception handler list\n\nParameters:\n- pSize (uint*): Size in bytes to allocate (or NULL for default 0x10)\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Allocated memory pointer, or indirectly via HeapAlloc\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3, 0x2: Heap version identifiers\n- 0xf: Alignment mask for 16-byte boundary\n- 0x10: Default allocation size when input is NULL\n- g_nHeapVersion: Global heap version flag\n- g_hHeapManager: Global heap handle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
