      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionIndex9",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionIndex9(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Leaves critical section at index 9, releasing the mutex for heap allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push mutex index 9 onto stack as parameter\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex to release the critical section\n3. Pop return address from stack (stdcall cleanup)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EAX contains heap allocator context (implicit from prior AcquireMutex call)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\nThis is a thin wrapper around LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex(9) used during heap deallocation.",
