      "name": "ConvertCharacterCase",
      "signature": "uint ConvertCharacterCase(void * this, void * pThis, uint dwCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Converts character code to lowercase using encoding-aware lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If encoding mode is disabled: simple ASCII A-Z to a-z conversion (0x41-0x5A -> add 0x20)\n2. If encoding mode is active:\n   - For chars < 0x100: check lookup table flag, optionally call encoding function\n   - Assemble high byte + low byte conversion based on 0x80 flag\n   - Call FUN_6f9eb792 converter for multi-byte processing\n   - Extract result as 1 or 2 bytes based on conversion mode\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Encoding context/mode pointer (ECX register, __thiscall)\n- dwCharCode (uint): Input character code\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Lowercase character code (same byte width as input)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cc0e19248bdb90cb6bf790db102f9ddf",
