      "name": "ClearBitRange",
      "signature": "void ClearBitRange(dword * pdwBitArray, int nStartBit)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Clears a range of bits in a bit array starting from the given bit index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate starting dword and bit offset from nStartBit\n2. Clear bits in the starting dword from bit offset to end\n3. Loop backward through preceding dwords, clearing all bits\n4. Stop early if no bits are set (optimization)\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBitArray (dword*): Pointer to bit array (array of 32-bit dwords)\n- nStartBit (int): Starting bit index to clear from\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per dword\n- 0x1f: Bitmask for bit position (modulo 32)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
