      "name": "ConvertDoubleToMantissaExponent",
      "signature": "void ConvertDoubleToMantissaExponent(uint * pMantissaExponent, uint * pdwDouble)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a 64-bit IEEE double to 48-bit mantissa/exponent format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent from bits [16:27] of upper word\n2. Check for zero, denormalized, or infinity special cases\n3. Adjust exponent bias from IEEE (0x3ff) to target (0x3c01)\n4. Combine sign bit, mantissa, and adjusted exponent\n5. Normalize mantissa using left shifts until MSB is set\n\nParameters:\n- pMantissaExponent (uint*): Pointer to output array [mantissa_lo, mantissa_hi, exponent_sign]\n- pdwDouble (uint*): Pointer to IEEE 64-bit double as [mantissa, exponent_sign_hi]\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff0: Exponent mask (11 bits)\n- 0xfffff: 20-bit mantissa mask\n- 0x3c01: Denormalized exponent bias\n- 0x3c00: Normalized exponent offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
