      "name": "ByteAlignedStringCopy",
      "signature": "uint * ByteAlignedStringCopy(uint * pszDest, uint * pszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Byte-aligned string copy with optimized null termination detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align source to 4-byte boundary if needed, copying unaligned leading bytes\n2. Scan source using aligned DWORD reads with null-byte detection mask (0xfefefeff trick)\n3. Copy aligned DWORDs to destination until null byte detected\n4. Handle final 1-3 unaligned bytes based on null byte position\n5. Return pointer to destination\n\nParameters:\n- pszDest (char*): Destination buffer (unaligned start allowed)\n- pszSrc (char*): Source string (unaligned start allowed)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to pszDest\n\nPerformance Note:\nUses aligned word-size reads and null-detection mask to avoid per-byte checks.",
