      "name": "AllocateMemoryWithHeap",
      "signature": "int * AllocateMemoryWithHeap(uint dwWidth, uint dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory with width*height dimensions using available heap managers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total size (dwWidth * dwHeight)\n2. Align size to 16-byte boundary using (size + 0xF) & 0xFFFFFFF0\n3. Try custom heap version 3 if available and size <= v3 limit\n4. Allocate from heap v3 and clear memory with memset\n5. Fall back to heap version 2 if available and aligned size <= v2 limit\n6. Allocate from heap v2 using stride >> 4 calculation\n7. Fall back to system HeapAlloc(g_hHeapManager) with 16K alignment flag\n8. If allocation fails and memory recovery enabled, invoke GC and retry loop\n\nParameters:\n- dwWidth: Width dimension in elements\n- dwHeight: Height dimension in elements\n- IMPLICIT: EBX preserves exception context, FS:[0x0] points to exception list\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory on success (cleared to zero)\n- NULL on failure (when recovery disabled or GC exhausted)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:371cf2604575a233020cd5d20fe5277c",
