      "name": "CompareFpuExtendedValues",
      "signature": "uint CompareFpuExtendedValues(int nMantissaLowA, uint dwMantissaHighA, ushort wExponentA, uint dwUnused, uint dwMantissaHighB, uint dwExponentB)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Compares two IEEE 754 extended precision (float10) floating-point values.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - FPU comparison helper for math library.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reconstruct float10 value A from split parameters (mantissa low/high + exponent)\n2. Check if value A mantissa high bit indicates normalized form\n3. If both mantissa parts are zero, return 0 (equal/zero comparison)\n4. Extract exponent bits (mask 0x7fff) from value A, return if non-zero\n5. Check exponent of value B - handle special cases (0 = denormal, 0x7fff = infinity/NaN)\n6. Scale value A by g_ldFpuScaleFactor constant and extract new components\n7. For normalized values, compute classification from upper mantissa bits\n8. Use lookup table g_abExponentClassLookup to determine special value type\n9. Return appropriate comparison result or classification code\n\nParameters:\n- nMantissaLowA (int): Low 32 bits of value A mantissa\n- dwMantissaHighA (uint): High 32 bits of value A mantissa\n- wExponentA (ushort): 15-bit biased exponent + sign of value A\n- dwUnused (uint): Padding/unused (float10 stack alignment)\n- dwMantissaHighB (uint): High mantissa bits of value B for comparison\n- dwExponentB (uint): Exponent bits of value B\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Values are equal or both zero\n- Non-zero: Exponent or classification code indicating comparison result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Both mantissa parts zero: Returns 0 immediately\n- Exponent 0x7fff: Infinity or NaN detected\n- Uses lookup table at 0x6f9f10f0 for exponent classification\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fff: Exponent mask (15 bits, excludes sign)\n- 0xe000000: Upper mantissa classification mask\n- 0x1c: Bit shift for lookup table index (28 bits right)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:35a926809c02214f1c021da8fe53c5e6",
