      "name": "Memmove",
      "signature": "void * Memmove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, dword nCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies memory from source to destination with overlap handling (memmove behavior).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if source and destination overlap (pDest < pSrc < pDest + nCount)\n2. If overlap detected, copy backwards from end to start\n3. Otherwise, copy forwards from start to end\n4. Use optimized dword-aligned copying when possible (8+ dwords)\n5. Handle partial dwords (1-3 bytes) via byte copying\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination memory address\n- pSrc (void*): Source memory address\n- nCount (dword): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to destination (pDest)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Overlapping regions: Uses backwards copy to prevent data corruption\n- Unaligned addresses: Falls back to byte-by-byte copy\n- Zero-length: Returns destination immediately",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bff09423b51fd121ea30afec957819f4",
