      "name": "ParseIntegerString",
      "signature": "void ParseIntegerString(void * this, byte * pszString, int * pnResult, void * pnRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Wrapper to parse integer string with heap selection validation. Delegates to FUN_6f9ea25c.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push 0x0 (error flags parameter) onto stack\n2. Push pnRadix (radix/base for conversion)\n3. Push pnResult (output buffer pointer)\n4. Push pszString (input string pointer)\n5. Call FUN_6f9ea25c(this, pszString, pnResult, pnRadix, 0x0)\n6. Clean up 4 parameters from stack (ADD ESP, 0x10)\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- this (void *): Implementation context (typically ECX in __thiscall)\n- pszString (byte *): Null-terminated input string to parse\n- pnResult (int *): Output buffer for parsed integer result\n- pnRadix (void *): Base/radix (8=octal, 10=decimal, 16=hex)\n\nReturns:\n- void (actual result stored via pnResult output parameter)",
