      "name": "FreeAllocationBlock",
      "signature": "void FreeAllocationBlock(dword * pdwAllocInfo, int nBlockOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Deallocates a block from the V3 heap pool, updating linked-list structure and freeing pages when all allocations in a page are freed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract allocation block size and metadata from block header\n2. Check block's buddy block and merge if both are free\n3. Update linked-list pointers to remove block from allocations\n4. Update allocation count and flag bits for the page\n5. If page becomes completely free, deallocate it via VirtualFree\n\nParameters:\n- pdwAllocInfo (uint*): Pointer to allocation pool metadata\n- nBlockOffset (int): Offset to block header relative to pool base\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xf (15): Block size alignment shift\n- 0x3f (63): Maximum allocation class\n- 0x20 (32): Threshold for switching allocation class registers\n- 0x204 (516): Page control structure size\n- 0x144 (324): Offset to allocation class manager",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ef5171f8f7487cff01081036951ae8fa",
