      "name": "HeapAllocateBlock",
      "signature": "int * HeapAllocateBlock(dword * pdwHeapBlocks)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from the V3 buddy heap allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 16-byte boundary (0x10)\n2. Calculate high and low bitmasks for buddy size classification\n3. Search heap forward then backward for free block of matching size\n4. If no suitable block found, attempt heap expansion via defragmentation\n5. Calculate buddy index based on available blocks\n6. Check bitmap to find first available buddy slot\n7. Split larger blocks if necessary (size adjustment)\n8. Update bitmap accounting and buddy list linkage\n9. Return pointer to allocated block (offset by +1)\n\nParameters:\n- pdwHeapBlocks (uint *): Size of memory to allocate in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Non-NULL pointer: Allocated memory block ready for use\n- NULL: Allocation failed (out of memory or defragmentation failed)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
