      "name": "InitializeHeapPage",
      "signature": "int InitializeHeapPage(int nHeapData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new 32KB heap page in the buddy allocator system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate buddy index (power of 2) from heap metadata\n2. Initialize free list headers (63 buddy slots) with self-references\n3. Allocate 32KB (0x8000) virtual memory page using Windows VirtualAlloc\n4. Partition page into 256-byte blocks (0x100 chunks), linking doubly in free lists\n5. Update heap metadata: clear page availability bit, increment page count, mark memory block initialized\n6. Return buddy index (-1 on allocation failure)\n\nParameters:\n- pHeapData (int): Pointer to heap metadata structure containing page pointers and bitmap\n\nReturns:\n- >=0: Buddy index of newly allocated page (0-based)\n- -1: VirtualAlloc failed, page allocation unsuccessful\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8000 (32768): Page size in bytes\n- 0x204: Distance between buddy metadata entries (includes padding)\n- 0x144: Offset to first buddy metadata from page info base\n- 0x1c00: Last valid block address in page (for iteration boundary)\n- 0x3f (63): Number of buddy slots (log2 sizes from 16 to 2GB)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0002c858ef3942a0b403454c72674bfe",
