      "name": "InitializeMemoryPool",
      "signature": "void * * InitializeMemoryPool(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize game memory pool with heap and virtual memory allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if heap already initialized (g_dwHeapInitialized == -1)\n2. If not, allocate 0x2020 bytes from heap manager\n3. Allocate 0x400000 bytes virtual memory at any address with 0x400 page size\n4. Commit first 0x10000 bytes (0x1000 = PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE)\n5. Initialize 0x400 pool entries with stride=0x20 bytes each\n6. Zero out and link memory blocks for allocation tracking\n7. Return pointer to pool header structure\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Uses global heap manager (g_hHeapManager)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwHeapInitialized flag for singleton initialization\n\nReturns:\n- void **: Pointer to memory pool header on success, NULL on failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b10e654b1e0872dc227e39198444a376",
