      "name": "RemoveLoopNode",
      "signature": "void RemoveLoopNode(void * ppNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked loop list, updating head pointer if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Free virtual memory (offset +0x10) if allocated\n2. Update loop head pointer (PTR_PTR_LOOP_6f9f3390) if removing first node\n3. Unlink from doubly-linked list by updating forward/backward pointers\n4. Free heap memory for node or mark special loop node as deleted\n\nParameters:\n- ppNode (void*): Pointer to doubly-linked list node structure with:\n  - Offset +0x0: Next pointer (for forward link)\n  - Offset +0x4: Previous pointer (for backward link)\n  - Offset +0x10: Virtual memory allocation to free\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6f9f3390: Global loop head pointer\n- 0x6f9f1370: Special loop node address (terminal marker)\n- 0x6f9f1380: Deletion flag for special node\n- 0x8000: MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:54ffff5ceafbb1247d2270b70dfe4f31",
