      "name": "AllocateFromMemoryPool",
      "signature": "int * AllocateFromMemoryPool(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a managed pool with size alignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search existing memory pools for matching size allocation\n2. If found in current pool, update tracking and return allocation\n3. If not found, search all pools for compatible space\n4. If no space available, allocate new memory pool via VirtualAlloc\n5. Initialize new pool structure and link into memory pool chain\n6. Return aligned pointer to allocated memory\n\nParameters:\n- nSize (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- int*: Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x806: Pool size limit (2054 entries)\n- 0x1000 (4096): Page-aligned allocation size\n- 0x400 (1024): Stride between tracking entries\n- 0x3d: Initialization marker byte offset\n- 0xf0, 0xf1: Pool entry markers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:de76025ed2839a23b964285c7e0d5701",
