      "name": "AllocatePoolBlock",
      "signature": "int AllocatePoolBlock(int * pPool, uint dwPoolSize, uint dwBlockSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a block of specified size in a memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pool metadata from first two uint fields and buffer end address\n2. Search for free space by scanning null-terminated free block chains\n3. Track consecutive null bytes (zero-count) to find large enough gaps\n4. If space found before end, allocate and update pool pointer\n5. Otherwise fail (return 0)\n6. Mark allocated block with given byte value at start\n7. Return encoded pointer (pool pointer * 0x10 - param_1 * 0xf)\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (int*): Pointer to pool metadata [buffer_ptr, used_size, ...]\n- nPoolSize (uint): Available pool size in bytes\n- nBlockSize (uint): Requested block size to allocate\n\nReturns:\n- Encoded pointer to allocated block, or 0 on failure\n\nStructure Layout:\n- pPool[0]: Current buffer pointer\n- pPool[1]: Used/offset value\n- pPool[2]: Buffer start\n- pPool[0x3e]: Buffer end address\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10, -0xf: Encoding multipliers for return value\n- 8: Offset for next allocation attempt",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4f3543287939943021eaf1632a1582f1",
