      "name": "LocaleMapStringWithConversion",
      "signature": "int LocaleMapStringWithConversion(LCID locale, dword dwMapFlags, char * szSrcA, int nSrcLenA, wchar_t * wszDstW, int nDstLenW, dword dwCodePage, int nUseDefault)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Maps a string with locale-aware character conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception list for SEH (Structured Exception Handling)\n2. If locale mode not cached, probe API capabilities (LCMapStringW, LCMapStringA)\n3. Cache result: 1=Unicode capable, 2=ANSI only\n4. Validate source string length using FindStringLength\n5. If ANSI-only mode: call LCMapStringA directly with mapped result\n6. If Unicode mode: convert ANSI to wide on stack, apply locale mapping, convert back\n\nParameters:\n- locale (LCID): Windows locale identifier for case/collation rules\n- dwMapFlags (dword): Mapping flags (0x100=case, 0x400=output as Unicode)\n- szSrcA (char*): ANSI source string\n- nSrcLenA (int): Source length in bytes\n- wszDstW (wchar_t*): Output buffer for mapped string\n- nDstLenW (int): Output buffer size in characters\n- dwCodePage (dword): Multibyte code page (CP_ACP if 0)\n- nUseDefault (int): Use default char for unmappable chars\n\nReturns:\n- Mapped string length on success (characters in destination encoding)\n- 0 on failure (buffer too small, invalid parameters, or API unavailable)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: LCMapString case mapping flag\n- 0x400: Output as Unicode flag\n- 0x220: WideCharToMultiByte flags (composed + no default + no usage)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c1d05e132bc8c3bc87e7a971916e9b9b",
