      "name": "BigIntMultiplyAccumulate",
      "signature": "void BigIntMultiplyAccumulate(char * szData, int nCount, uint * pdwResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Multiply 96-bit accumulator by each byte of input string and normalize result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 96-bit result to 0 and exponent to 0x404e\n2. For each input byte, shift result left by 8 bits\n3. Add current byte multiplied into result via ___add_12\n4. After processing all bytes, normalize by shifting left until high bit set\n5. Store final exponent in result offset 10\n\nParameters:\n- szData (char*): Input string of bytes to multiply\n- nCount (int): Number of bytes to process from input\n- pdwResult (uint*): Pointer to 96-bit result array [lo, mid, hi]\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pdwResult array and offset 10)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
