      "name": "ConvertCharacterToLocalEncoding",
      "signature": "uint ConvertCharacterToLocalEncoding(void * this, void * pThis, uint dwCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Converts a character code to local encoding, handling both ASCII and multi-byte character sets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character table mode is ASCII-only\n2. If ASCII mode, apply simple offset for lowercase conversion (0x60-0x7a)\n3. If multi-byte mode, lookup character in g_pCharLookupTable\n4. Extract high/low bytes and determine byte count (1 or 2)\n5. Call LocaleMapStringWithConversion to map bytes to encoded output\n6. Extract result from pOutputBuffer and return mapped character\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): Pointer to character conversion context/state\n- dwCharCode (uint): Input character code to convert\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Converted character code, or original if no conversion applied",
