      "name": "strcmp",
      "signature": "int strcmp(char * lpszStr1, char * lpszStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "MSVC CRT strcmp - Compare two null-terminated ANSI strings lexicographically.\n\nClassification: Leaf function, CRT library routine\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if lpszStr1 is DWORD-aligned (address & 3)\n2. If bit 0 set (odd address), compare single byte, advance pointers\n3. If bit 1 set (2-byte misaligned), compare 2 bytes via WORD read\n4. Enter main loop: read 4 bytes from lpszStr1 at once (DWORD optimization)\n5. Compare each of 4 bytes against lpszStr2:\n   - Byte 0: low byte of DWORD\n   - Byte 1: bits 8-15 (>> 8)\n   - Byte 2: bits 16-23 (>> 16)  \n   - Byte 3: bits 24-31 (>> 24)\n6. On mismatch or null terminator found, exit loop\n7. Return: 0 if equal, negative if lpszStr1 < lpszStr2, positive otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  lpszStr1 - First string to compare (char *)\n  lpszStr2 - Second string to compare (char *)\n\nReturns:\n  0 if strings are equal\n  Negative value if lpszStr1 < lpszStr2 (lexicographically)\n  Positive value if lpszStr1 > lpszStr2\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles unaligned string addresses via byte/word prefix comparisons\n  - Optimized for aligned memory access (DWORD reads in main loop)\n  - Empty strings return 0 (both start with null terminator)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f93a26193b15127770b523718dea2fb3",
