      "name": "CompareStringCaseInsensitive",
      "signature": "int CompareStringCaseInsensitive(byte * pbString1, char * szString2, int nLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive string comparison with length limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If length is 0, return immediately (0)\n2. If character table mode is 0: Compare characters directly with case conversion\n   - Convert uppercase (0x41-0x5A) to lowercase by adding 0x20\n   - Compare converted bytes; stop on null terminator or length exhausted\n3. If mode != 0: Use mutex-protected character conversion table\n   - Increment ref count, acquire mutex if table protected\n   - Call ConvertCharacterCase for each character pair\n   - Decrement ref count or leave critical section on completion\n\nParameters:\n- pbString1 (byte *): First string to compare\n- szString2 (char *): Second string to compare\n- nLength (int): Maximum comparison length\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Strings are equal up to length\n- -1: First string is less than second (first byte < second byte)\n- 1: First string is greater than second (first byte > second byte)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:662566ebcde3842108cf876001e2ae79",
