      "name": "_aulldiv",
      "signature": "ulonglong _aulldiv(ulonglong qwDividend, ulonglong qwDivisor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "_aulldiv - Unsigned 64-bit Integer Division (CRT Helper)\n\nMicrosoft C Runtime helper function for 64-bit unsigned integer division.\nThis is a compiler-generated intrinsic that divides two 64-bit unsigned values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If divisor fits in 32 bits (high DWORD is 0):\n   a. Perform simple 32-bit division in sequence\n   b. Divide high dividend by divisor -> result high\n   c. Divide (remainder:low dividend) by divisor -> result low\n2. If divisor is 64 bits:\n   a. Shift both dividend and divisor right until divisor fits in 32 bits\n   b. Perform trial division\n   c. Verify result by multiplication and adjust if needed\n\nParameters (on stack, 16 bytes total):\n  [ESP+4]  dwDividendLow  - Low 32 bits of 64-bit dividend\n  [ESP+8]  dwDividendHigh - High 32 bits of 64-bit dividend\n  [ESP+12] dwDivisorLow   - Low 32 bits of 64-bit divisor\n  [ESP+16] dwDivisorHigh  - High 32 bits of 64-bit divisor\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX - 64-bit quotient (EDX=high, EAX=low)\n\nCalling Convention: __cdecl (caller cleans stack)\n  - Cleanup: RET 0x10 (16 bytes, 4 DWORDs)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - _aullrem @ 0x6f9ecfc0: Unsigned 64-bit modulo (same parameters)\n  - _alldiv: Signed 64-bit division\n  - _allrem: Signed 64-bit modulo\n\nNote: Function boundaries are broken in Ghidra database. Actual code spans\n      0x6f9ecf50 to 0x6f9ecfbd (RET 0x10). Disassembly shows only entry point.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
