      "name": "_aullrem",
      "signature": "ulonglong _aullrem(uint dwDividendLow, uint dwDividendHigh, uint dwDivisorLow, uint dwDivisorHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Microsoft Visual C++ runtime 64-bit unsigned modulo helper function (_aullrem).\nComputes the remainder of dividing a 64-bit unsigned integer by another 64-bit unsigned integer.\nThis is a compiler-generated CRT routine, not application code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If divisor high word (dwDivisorHigh) is zero:\n   a. Perform fast path using two consecutive 32-bit DIV instructions\n   b. First divide dwDividendHigh by dwDivisorLow to get intermediate remainder\n   c. Concatenate remainder with dwDividendLow and divide again by dwDivisorLow\n   d. Return remainder as 64-bit value with high word zero\n2. For full 64-bit divisor (dwDivisorHigh != 0):\n   a. Normalize both dividend and divisor by right-shifting until divisor high is zero\n   b. Count shifts needed to clear divisor high bits\n   c. Perform trial division with normalized values to estimate quotient\n   d. Multiply trial quotient by original divisor\n   e. Compare product with dividend; if product > dividend, subtract divisor once\n   f. Compute remainder as dividend minus adjusted product\n\nParameters:\n  dwDividendLow (uint, Stack[0x4]) - Low 32 bits of 64-bit dividend\n  dwDividendHigh (uint, Stack[0x8]) - High 32 bits of 64-bit dividend\n  dwDivisorLow (uint, Stack[0xc]) - Low 32 bits of 64-bit divisor\n  dwDivisorHigh (uint, Stack[0x10]) - High 32 bits of 64-bit divisor\n\nReturns:\n  ulonglong - 64-bit remainder (dividend % divisor) in EDX:EAX\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  uVar1 (qwTrialQuotient) - Trial quotient from normalized division\n  lVar2 (llProductDivisorLow) - Product of quotient and divisor low\n  uVar3 (dwShiftedDividendLow) - Dividend low during normalization loop\n  uVar4 (dwProductHigh) - High word of quotient * divisor product\n  uVar5 (dwShiftedDivisorHigh) - Divisor high during normalization\n  iVar6 (nRemainderLow) - Low 32 bits of computed remainder\n  iVar7 (nRemainderHigh) - High 32 bits of computed remainder\n  uVar8 (dwShiftedDividendHigh) - Dividend high during normalization\n  uVar9 (dwProductLow) - Low word of product, later used as temp\n  uVar10 (dwProductHighSum) - Sum of product components for comparison\n  bVar11 (fBorrowFlag) - Borrow flag from subtraction\n\nCalling Convention: __cdecl (caller cleans stack, RET 0x10)\n\nClassification: Leaf function, compiler-generated CRT helper",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e318b2efa2b7ed9dcb619fe5ba3fc2d5",
