      "name": "DivideDoubleWithSpill",
      "signature": "uint DivideDoubleWithSpill(uint dwDoubleLow, uint dwDoubleHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs double division with FPU stack spill handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if divisor exponent indicates NaN/Infinity (0x7ff00000 mask)\n2. If special value, perform direct FDIV and return\n3. Check FPU status word for pending FPU stack values (0x3800 mask)\n4. If FPU stack has values, spill them before division\n5. Otherwise exchange ST0/ST1, spill top, load divisor, divide, restore\n\nParameters:\n- dwDoubleLow (uint): Low 32 bits of double divisor\n- dwDoubleHigh (uint): High 32 bits of double divisor (contains exponent)\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains dividend, ST1 may contain value to preserve\n\nReturns:\n- Result in ST0 after division, EAX passed through\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff00000: IEEE 754 double exponent mask for NaN/Infinity\n- 0x3800: FPU status word mask for stack top pointer (bits 11-13)",
